.TH PUTC 3
.SH NAME
putc, putchar, fputc \- put a character on a stream
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <stdio.h>

int
putc(c, stream)
int c;
FILE *stream;

int
putchar(c)
int c;

int
fputc(c, stream)
int c;
FILE *stream;
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B putc
writes the character
.I c
on
.IR stream .
.B putchar(c)
is
.BR "putc(c, stdout)" .
.B fputc
does what
.B putc
does, as a function instead of a macro.
.SH "RETURN VALUES"
The character written, or EOF if it could not be written. Since putc
writes into the stream's buffer, a failure may show only later, when
the buffer is written out: check
.BR ferror (3),
or the result of
.BR fflush (3)
or
.BR fclose (3),
at the end.
.SH SEE ALSO
puts(3), printf(3), fwrite(3), fclose(3), ferror(3), getc(3), stdio(3)
.SH HISTORY
The
.B putc
function first appeared in Version 1 AT&T UNIX,
.B putchar
in Version 2, and
.B fputc
in Version 7.
.SH BUGS
Since
.B putc
is a macro, it evaluates
.I stream
more than once.
